        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "Despite my general dislike for faceless skyscrapers and congested office blocks towering into the sky, I somehow loved this view of the Toronto skyline and didn't want to leave! A comfortable seat on a bench on the lakeside only reinforced my reluctance to get up and get back to the ferry wharf! This is the last shot of the classic Toronto skyline that features is so many publications about Toronto. Although there are many places in town where you can catch this skyline, arguably the best view of the Toronto skyline would have to be from the Toronto Islands. It's easy to get there too. Go to the town docks and take a short 10 minute ferry crossing to get there. It's also a lovely place to spend the the day. I did just that- I'm now on Ward's Island and all my previous few pictures were from here. This view is even better in the late evening or at dusk, but it would probably be too cold to stand here plus a tripod would have been in order, which I do not own. There was no stump or railing either where I could rest my camera. So a day shot it had to be then,and this is it. (Toronto, Canada, Nov.2015)",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
